  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="6f78e593-7f81-5449-b4b0-b6ba8367d3bb" activityNameId="228fe0ab-e248-5d07-be88-70c3beac5ed0" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ash from paper prod. sludge, 0% water, to residual material landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ash from paper prod. sludge, 0% water, to residual material landfill
Inventoried waste contains 100% composition of paper sludge ash; . waste composition (wet, in ppm): H2O n.a.; O 30083; H n.a.; C 9164.7; S 41259; N 6222.5; P 146230; B n.a.; Cl 0.012408; Br n.a.; F 9.6141; I n.a.; Ag n.a.; As 10.215; Ba n.a.; Cd 1.5403; Co 32.145; Cr 98.271; Cu 560.17; Hg 1.0175; Mn 1069.5; Mo 22.403; Ni 60.085; Pb 267.55; Sb n.a.; Se n.a.; Sn 79.568; V n.a.; Zn 865.8; Be n.a.; Sc n.a.; Sr n.a.; Ti n.a.; Tl n.a.; W n.a.; Si 199030; Fe 158420; Ca 221030; Al 50413; K 14897; Mg 29415; Na 90757; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 100%. ;; UUID: 0092d7e5-7796-430d-8a7a-5c7080655ab5
Waste-specific short-term emissions to water from leachate. Long-term emissions from landfill to ground water. 
Location: Technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Landfill includes base seal and leachate collection system.
Technology: Swiss residual material landfill for polluted, inorganic waste. With base seal and leachate collection system. Recultivation after closure. 
Time period: Waste composition as given in literature reference, theoretical data or other source. Transfer coefficients from prospective model.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Landfill model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial waste composition from various literature sources. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions until the next glacial period occurs (in 60'000a) and the landfill is eroded. Maximal long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material (except Cr). Minimal long-term emissions are derived implicitly from the mean and maximal values assuming a lognormal distribution.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_0092d7e5-7796-430d-8a7a-5c7080655ab5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
